bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    scv_snapshot_recover_deletes_live_foreign_staging_2026_11_09, 1, "process_is_running (rt_process_is_running) only answers for children in this process's SPAWNED_CHILDREN registry (env_process.rs:1269); measured process_is_running(getpid()) = false on Windows. recover_v1 (compile_snapshot_retention_v1.spl:26-36) therefore treats EVERY foreign .tmp.<pid> staging dir as abandoned and dir_remove()s it, racing a concurrent lane's publish."
    scv_snapshot_recover_deletes_live_foreign_staging_2026_11_09, 2, "Fix direction: probe with process_exists (arbitrary-PID). Not switched in PR #8001 because src/app/test/package_index_acceptance_snapshot.spl:118-135 uses an exited-but-registered child pid as the abandoned owner; on Windows process_exists may report it alive while the registry holds its handle. That fixture must change together with the probe. Found while fixing stage2_positional_native_build_fails_in_capsule_collection_2026-09-06."
    scv_snapshot_recover_deletes_live_foreign_staging_2026_11_09, 3, "bootp2 2026-11-09: recover now probes with process_exists; fixture picks a process_exists-dead owner and asserts live foreign (pid 4/1) staging preserved. PR #8084. Red: removed=2 (live pid 4 deleted); green: removed=1."

bugs |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    scv_snapshot_recover_deletes_live_foreign_staging_2026_11_09, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "scv_compile_snapshot_recover_v1 probes foreign .tmp.<pid> staging owners with process_is_running (owned-children only), so a live concurrent builder looks dead and its staging dir can be deleted mid-publish", src/lib/scv/compile_snapshot_retention_v1.spl, 26, src/lib/scv/compile_snapshot_retention_v1.spl, 2026-11-09, 2026-11-09, true

